          "caption": "Hex box"
        }
      ],
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "Why I built it",
          "body": "Every Packaging Design assignment starts with a dieline. Drawing each net by hand from a 3D model was slow and easy to get wrong, so I built a tool that unfolds the model for me."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "media/dielineforge/app.jpg",
          "w": 1400,
          "h": 1045,
          "caption": "The drop page: model in, dieline out."
        },
        {
          "type": "stats",
          "items": [
            {
              "n": 8,
              "label": "3D file formats it reads"
            },
            {
              "n": 7,
              "label": "dieline layers"
            },
            {
              "n": 0,
              "label": "cloud services needed"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How it works",
          "body": "Blender runs in the background and unfolds the model with its Paper Model extension. The output is a layered SVG and PDF at 1:1, with cut, mountain crease, valley crease, glue, bleed and registration on separate layers."
        },
        {
          "type": "gallery",
          "items": [
            {
