        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "The problem",
          "body": "The JBL Headphones app does not run on Apple silicon Macs, so switching noise cancelling meant picking up an iPad."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "src": "media/jbl-control/menubar.jpg",
          "w": 1800,
          "h": 520,
          "caption": "Noise cancelling, ambient, talk-through and off."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "title": "How",
          "body": "The headphones use an Airoha chip that speaks the RACE protocol over a Bluetooth serial channel. I decoded the mode commands and built a menu-bar app around them, with URL shortcuts for automation."
        }
      ]
